# GhostCrab Integration SOP Editor (Cursor)

## When to use

Use this rule when editing `ghostcrab-integrations/*/sop*.md` files or when the user asks to clean a GhostCrab/MindBrain integration SOP export.

## Composer 2.5 rule

Edit only the introduction unless the user explicitly asks for a full rewrite.

## Procedure

1. Find SOP files:

```bash
find ghostcrab-integrations -maxdepth 2 -type f -iname 'sop*.md'
```

2. Read the first 80 to 160 lines.
3. Identify the first real technical section to preserve.
4. Remove only the export opening:
   - Perplexity logo
   - raw task prompt
   - generic pitch
   - filler sentence
   - link-only heading
   - decorative separator immediately after the export prompt
5. Write a new introduction with the template below.
6. Place the preserved technical body after the new introduction.
7. Keep exactly one blank line between Markdown blocks.

## Introduction template

```markdown
# Integrating mindBrain with {framework_name}

## About {framework_name}

{Two to four concise sentences and one official link.}

## MindBrain

MindBrain is a structured agentic database that makes any domain navigable in real time - its intelligence lives in schema enforcement, typed ontologies, and pre-computed projections that cost zero inference at query time.

## Why integrate mindBrain with {framework_name}

{One or two framework-specific paragraphs.}

## SKILLS available in this repo

{Two or three local skill files when they exist.}
```

## Do not

- Do not rewrite code blocks.
- Do not remove citations or footnotes.
- Do not invent framework capabilities.
- Do not use third-party sources when an official source is available.
- Do not claim a local skill is installed automatically.

## Final check

Before finishing, verify:

- raw prompt removed
- official framework link present
- MindBrain definition exact
- technical body preserved
- local skill list accurate
